# BuildKit named-context trim for riir-chaind builds (deploy/Dockerfile,
# Issue 028 analysis, 2026-08-22). This repo arrives as a named context
# (`--build-context katgpt-rs=../katgpt-rs`); BuildKit applies THIS file at
# the context root. Without it the context ships .git/ (184 MB) — and on a
# local builder, target/ (tens of GB).
#
# The daemon build compiles ZERO katgpt crates (measured: `cargo tree -p
# riir-chaind --bin riir-chaind` — the context exists for manifest
# resolution only), so nothing here is load-bearing for that image beyond
# Cargo.toml manifests + declared target files.

target/
**/target/
.git/
.github/

# Lean toolchain artifacts — the daemon image does not need the proofs.
.proofs/
**/.lake/
**/.agents/

# Docs and research the build has no use for.
.benchmarks/
.research/
.issues/
.plans/
.proposals/
.docs/
**/node_modules/

# NOT excluded, deliberately: `tests/`, `examples/`, `benches/` — workspace
# manifests declare `[[test]]`/`[[example]]`/`[[bench]]` targets by name, and
# cargo fails at MANIFEST LOAD if a declared target's file is missing (the
# riir-chain .dockerignore lesson).

# Local editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
